    preview: "Seoul – South Korea’s top court overturned former prime minister Han Duck-soo’s 15-year sentence on Thursday for aiding a martial law declaration that briefly suspended civilian rule, sending the case back to a lower court. The 2024 decree issued by the president at the time, Yoon Suk Yeol, plunged the country into chaos, but lasted only around six hours as opposition lawmakers scrambled to overturn it in a vote.",
    body: "Seoul – South Korea’s top court overturned former prime minister Han Duck-soo’s 15-year sentence on Thursday for aiding a martial law declaration that briefly suspended civilian rule, sending the case back to a lower court.\n\nThe 2024 decree issued by the president at the time, Yoon Suk Yeol, plunged the country into chaos, but lasted only around six hours as opposition lawmakers scrambled to overturn it in a vote.\n\nHan, one of several top officials sentenced over the short-lived martial law bid, was handed a 23-year jail term in January for engaging in the declaration, which the court said threatened “the constitutional order” and amounted to insurrection.",
