    summary: "China issues 'peace declaration' agreed with Trump and Putin China has released a “peace declaration” it said its President Xi Jinping and his US and Russian counterparts Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin had agreed on at their unprecedented three-way meeting, where they said nuclear wars were futile and should never be fought. All three countries committed to maintaining strategic stability and international security, according to a four-point declaration published by Chinese official media Xinhua. The leaders reportedly discussed Russia's war in Ukraine and the US-Israeli war on Iran. The three countries will conduct a dialogue on reducing nuclear risks and preventing the proliferation of nuclear weapons, Xinhua said. The three heads of state also agreed on reform for a \"more effective\" United Nations, and said that the International Criminal Court and similar institutions must not abuse their jurisdiction, according to the declaration.",
